it doesn't seem like hogwarts legacy  will be hitting store shelves anytime  soon but did you know there's actually a  new harry potter video game that  released this year i know crazy right  honestly this is really bizarre to me  just how under the radar this game has  been so far you really have to be  looking for the information to find this  and i think one of the reasons is  because it still hasn't been released in  major territories like the united states  in europe but if you haven't heard harry  potter magic awaken is a wizarding world  video game that just recently had its  official launch but only in the  territories of china taiwan hong kong  and macau now from what i've read they  are planning to release in other  territories at some point including the  us the latest reports have indicated a  winter 2021 target for the territories  of thailand the philippines malaysia  singapore indonesia japan and south  korea but most of you listening to this  video right now at least according to my  analytics are from the americas and  europe so what about our territories  here americas and europe well there is a  sign that the us release could be  happening sooner than you may think so  make sure to stick around for that  because we'll definitely get into those  details before the end of the video as  far as the actual game itself goes this  is quite different from hogwarts legacy  it's an rpg card game for pc android and  ios and it's set 10 years after harry  potter's victory over voldemort in the  battle of hogwarts it was first  announced back in october of 2019 and is  being developed by netease and published  by wb under the port key games label  which yes this is the very same label  that hogwarts legacy will be published  under when it final releases hopefully  in 2022 so with magic awakens taking  place so close to the original series  there will actually be quite a few  familiar faces that we'll interact with  throughout the game our character's  journey starts similar to harry's when  the half giant rubius hagrid shows up to  deliver a letter of acceptance to a  young muggleborn hagrid then teaches  them about the wizarding world and joins  them on their first trip to diagon alley  the story really kicks off at the  sorting ceremony when a fellow first  year ivy warrington goes missing in  addition to solving that mystery players  will get to choose their hogwarts house  attend classes explore the castle and  even join the dueling club most of the  action and spell casting will be  centered on the game's card based combat  system normally i'll be honest i'm not  really into mobile games and i don't  play a lot of these card based strategy  rpg games but with this one being a  harry potter game they certainly have my  attention at the very least i will say  one thing i absolutely love about it  just from the videos i've seen just from  the trailer that you're seeing right now  is the art style it somehow manages to  nail that harry potter atmosphere and  overall sense of magic and wonder  despite being a rather refreshing take  on the series it kind of reminds me a  bit of the thai harry potter book covers  which are just absolutely gorgeous if  you haven't seen them i mean just look  at this probably my favorite covers out  of all the various hp translations now  even though it's technically a mobile  game they do actually have it for pc as  well so i was excited to see that they  have that in addition to the ios and  android versions which personally i  think this will really help the game  when it finally does release in the us  and europe and what's so bizarre to me  is how they're seemingly putting the us  the rest of the americas and europe on  the back burner despite the fact that  these are two of the biggest territories  for the harry potter franchise of course  there are certainly dynamics to the  mobile game market that i don't claim to  understand so maybe that has something  to do with it and why they're releasing  in certain territories before others and  of course it does take time to get an  accurate translation for the story and  all the dialogue they've created now i  mentioned at the start of the video that  there could be a sign the us release is  close or even imminent well it turns out  just a few weeks ago developer net ease  was holding interviews for the english  version of harry potter magic awakened  they were conducting two hour zoom  interviews with folks who could one  download the game to their phone two had  some mobile gaming experience and three  were fans of the harry potter series so  hopefully this is a sign that a full  release in the us and europe is much  closer than we think maybe even before  the end of 2021. of course the way  things are looking right now it is  really starting to seem like 2022 is  gonna be the year of harry potter at  least in the us hogwarts legacy the new  fantastic beasts movie and if this game  doesn't make it out here in 2021 then it  very well could be 2022 as well so it  could just be a massive year of harry  potter content which you know as fans  we're gonna absolutely love even though  i'd certainly like to get my hands on  the game a little bit sooner now  actually speaking of that though  you could play this game right now some  of you out there have actually already  played the game because it was in open  beta for a while unfortunately the  language barrier makes this harder for  those of us who only speak english but  i've talked with a few fans who have  actually played the game already in fact  you know what if you've already played  it be sure to leave a comment below and  let us know what you think so far is it  a harry potter game to keep on our radar  or is it not really worth your time how  have you found the overall mechanics of  the game let us know and if you're  interested in more harry potter content  be sure to check out the hogwarts legacy  playlist on the right side of your  screen now or if you're more in the mood  for some old school harry potter let's  plays then check out the playlist on the  left side of your screen as always thank  you all so much for watching i'll talk  to you again soon
 

